.el .ds Aq '
.TH bhtune-history-revert 1  "bhtune-history-revert "
.SH NAME
bhtune\-history\-revert \- Undo a run\*(Aqs PID write\-back, writing its recorded pre\-write P/I/D values back to the live loop. Reverts whichever `write`\-kind write\-back that run last recorded; refuses if the run has none, if that write\-back\*(Aqs pre\-read itself failed (nothing to revert to), or if the run did not use the `opcda` driver (nothing live to revert against)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-history\-revert\fR [\fB\-\-bridge\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIRUN_ID\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Undo a run\*(Aqs PID write\-back, writing its recorded pre\-write P/I/D values back to the live loop. Reverts whichever `write`\-kind write\-back that run last recorded; refuses if the run has none, if that write\-back\*(Aqs pre\-read itself failed (nothing to revert to), or if the run did not use the `opcda` driver (nothing live to revert against)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bridge\-host\fR \fI<BRIDGE_HOST>\fR
Cross\-checked against the run\*(Aqs own recorded bridge host \-\- never used to resolve a default, and deliberately has no `BHTUNE_BRIDGE_HOST`/config fallback the way every other command\*(Aqs `\-\-bridge\-host` does, so an unrelated ambient env var can never silently affect which gateway a revert targets. Omit this to use the recorded value; a value that contradicts it is refused rather than preferred, so a revert can never target a different gateway than the run it is undoing actually used (`db\-run\-request\-snapshot`)
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Cross\-checked against the run\*(Aqs own recorded OPC server \-\- never used to resolve a default. Omit this to use the recorded value; a value that contradicts it is refused rather than preferred, so a revert can never target a different server than the run it is undoing actually used (`db\-run\-request\-snapshot`)
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm writing to a live loop. Required \-\- there is no interactive prompt for reverting, since there is no calculated result to choose between as there is for `tune`\*(Aqs own write\-back step
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: table]
How to print the revert outcome
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Human\-readable text (default)
.IP \(bu 2
json: Pretty\-printed JSON. This is the external contract for scripted/scheduled consumers, so its shape must not change silently once shipped
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIRUN_ID\fR>

